TITLE: This Week’s US Stock Macro Outlook Highlights (August 3–7)

TEXT:
August 3 (Monday)
US releases July ISM Manufacturing PMI and June Construction Spending;
★★★★★ Palantir reports earnings after the close, focus on AI-driven growth, government/commercial contracts and AIP platform progress;
ON Semiconductor and Snap report earnings after the close.
August 4 (Tuesday)
US releases June JOLTS Job Openings, Trade Balance and Factory Orders;
★★★★★ AMD reports earnings after the close, key test of AI chip demand;
★★★★★SpaceX reports first earnings after listing after the close;
McDonald’s, Caterpillar and Pfizer report earnings pre-market.
August 5 (Wednesday)
US releases July ADP Employment Report and ISM Non-Manufacturing PMI;
★★★★Eli Lilly and Novo Nordisk report earnings pre-market, revealing latest weight-loss drug market dynamics;
★★★★ SanDisk and Western Digital report earnings after the close, focus on enterprise SSD, HBM and data-center storage demand;
★★★ Circle , Disney (pre-market), AppLovin , Figma and IonQ (after the close) report earnings.
August 6 (Thursday)
US releases weekly Initial Jobless Claims and Challenger layoff data;
★★★★★SpaceX unlocks approximately 9.115 billion shares, potential value nearly $100 billion, the largest single unlock in US history, testing liquidity;
Fed officials Musalem and Barkin speak;
★★★ AAOI and MP report earnings after the close.
August 7 (Friday)
★★★★★US releases July Nonfarm Payrolls (expected +90,000, previous +57,000) and Unemployment Rate (expected 4.3%, previous 4.2%); a reading above 100,000 could boost labor-market confidence and raise September rate-hike bets;
US releases New York Fed 1-Year Inflation Expectations and other data;
★★★ OKLO and VST report earnings pre-market.
*This week’s core US stock themes revolve around July nonfarm payrolls data, Fed officials’ signals, SpaceX’s first earnings and large-scale unlock, plus AI/storage earnings from AMD, SanDisk and Western Digital; market volatility is expected to intensify.
